@startuml
title A note hash built in two phases, in two execution contexts
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam componentBackgroundColor #EEF5FF
skinparam componentBorderColor #4A78B5
skinparam packageBackgroundColor #FAFCFF
skinparam packageBorderColor #4A78B5
skinparam ArrowColor #4A78B5
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #F5F9FF
skinparam noteBorderColor #4A78B5

package "Phase 1 — private execution" {
  component "owner\nwho gets paid" as OWN
  component "randomness\nfresh per note,\nblinds the owner" as RND
  component "partial_commitment:\nH(owner, randomness)" as PC
  component "validity commitment:\nH(partial_commitment,\ncompleter)" as VC
  OWN --> PC
  RND --> PC
  PC --> VC
}

package "Phase 2 — public or later private execution" {
  component "storage_slot" as SLOT
  component "value\nknown only now:\nthe swap rate, the\naccrued interest" as VAL
  component "note_hash:\nH(storage_slot,\npartial_commitment, value)" as NH
  SLOT --> NH
  VAL --> NH
}

PC --> NH : carried forward\nas an opaque Field
VC --> NH : must exist, or\ncompletion reverts

note bottom of VC
  Written to the nullifier tree, but with its
  own domain separator: it is not a note
  nullifier and consumes nothing. The tree
  is used here only as an append-only set
  whose entries can be proved to exist.
end note

note bottom of NH
  Every Aztec note is hashed this way, even
  when all fields are known in private. A note
  created in one step and a note completed in
  two produce the same hash.
end note
@enduml
